    public static void main(String[] args) {
        UrlBuilder urlBuilder = new UrlBuilder();
        String baseUrl = "https://example.co.uk/path/to/base";
        String relPath = "/path/to/resource";
        
        // Build absolute URL:
        String absoluteUrl = urlBuilder.getAbsolutePath(baseUrl, relPath);
        System.out.println(absoluteUrl);

        // Build relative URL:
        String relativeUrl = urlBuilder.getRelativeUrl(baseUrl, relPath);
        System.out.println(relativeUrl);
    }
}
```

In the above example, `getAbsolutePath` method is used to build an absolute URL from a base URL and a relative path. The `getRelativeUrl` method can be used to get the relative URL.

